# Dataset handling

- Download only via `uv run ir-spark-download` (Hugging Face snapshot `bigpictureio/companies-2023-q4-sm`, file `companies-2023-q4-sm.csv.gz`).
- Expected sha256 is pinned in `src/ir_spark/constants.py`. Do not "fix" a mismatch by skipping verification.
- Observed header: `handle,name,website,industry,size,type,founded,city,state,country_code`. There is no separate `domain` column; website is the URL-like field. LinkedIn is `handle` (company pages, not people).
- Local sample: `uv run ir-spark-sample` → `data/interim/companies_sample.csv` (gitignored). Local DQ: `uv run ir-spark-profile` → `data/processed/dq_summary.json` (aggregates only).
- Databricks: the full gzip is on UC Volume `/Volumes/workspace/default/ir_spark/companies-2023-q4-sm.csv.gz`. Do not use workspace files (500 MB cap) or DBFS root (disabled on Free Edition). Spark load is `notebooks/02_data_ingestion.py`. Delta: `workspace.ir_spark.companies_raw` (17,154,017) and `workspace.ir_spark.companies_sample` (30,000).
- Never print or commit full rows from the raw file in docs. Column names and aggregate counts are fine.
- License: Open Data Commons Attribution (ODC-By). Attribute BigPicture / the snapshot publisher; do not paste their marketing copy into the README.
